MODIFICATIONS A FAIRE :

[A] Now a bug report. The selection of Xpk-Mode is wrongly implemented. For
    some libraries you cannot select a corresponding mode. The Mode selection
    does not depend on XPKIF_MODES flag!!! I don't know who implemented this
    behaviour first, but it is nowhere documented.
    For example pseudo "USER" library supports different modes without different
    XpkMode structures. XPKIF_MODES tells, that there are different XpkMode
    structures, not that there are different modes!
    It would be fine, when ABackUp supports selection of USER mode directly,
    instead of selecting it in listview together with normal libraries.

[E] An other problem: In some cases ABackup finishes the backup after an error
    occured (for example disk error #20). In this cases ask the user, if he
    really wants to abort, or if he wants to restart with the first file on
    this disk. (Remember for that the file, you started the data on this
    disk. Recrunch all files starting with the first one the disk. If the
    first file was splitted, save only the part which isn't on previous
    disk.)

[E] Message si pb au lancement du prog de prefs

