[A] I noticed another "odd" thing. If I open the prefs editor on the
    Workbench screen (i.e. when ABackup isn't running), then it uses a
    fixed width font for the interface. When on the ABackup screen, it
    uses a proportional. Why? ;)

	If I start the ABackup-Preferences-Programm, I get
	Courier font. This is my favourite font, the same
	font which I get when I open a shell-window.
	I start the mainprogram ABackup, I get courier again.
	This is fine. But when I start the preferences-program
	from the main-program, I get the ugly Topaz font!
	Now I end both programs,(Prefs and Main).
	And now I start the Prefs-Program again.
	And I get Topaz font!
	This is really strange.
	But when I start the Mainprogram again, I get again
	courier font. But now it is impossible to get courier font
	in the Prefs-program. I have to make a reset, then I get
	courier again.
	First I thought that courier (13) is to large for
	the screen, but this can not be the reason, because
	I get it if I start the prefs program direct (by
	double-click) from virgin computer. Then I thought that
	maybe courier is locked
	in any way by the mainprogram. But this is not true, if
	I open a shell I always get courier. And the prefs-file
	in ENV: is not the reason, because the problem is still
	there if I delete it.
	It 's really a strange thing.

[G] Pb avec le prog de Prefs : si on l'appelle sur un écran
    public ou particulier, qu'on le "cache", qu'on ferme l'écran
    et qu'on le rappelle... il essaye de remettre sa fenêtre sur
    l'écran qui est fermé ! D'où enforcer hits en pagaille...

[A] When I set a preferences file with the tooltype PREFS in the
    main program's icon and start the program, these preferences
    only are known by the main program itself. When I then start
    the prefs program via gadged, it has the default settings. So
    if I want to make changes to my settings, I have to load my
    preferences file via the menu of the prefs program.

[A] A propos de ABackup, j'ai constaté un bug dans la version 5.00, que tu
    as peut-être corrigé depuis. J'ai décompacté l'archive dans un répertoire
    (en ram), j'ai lancé ABackup depuis ce répertoire, et j'ai joué avec.
    Quand j'ai quitté ABackup et que j'ai voulu effacer tout le répertoire,
    je n'ai pu effacer le répertoire ABackup. Cela signifie donc que tu
    effectues un "Lock" sur ce répertoire et que tu ne le libères pas. Ca
    n'est pas extrêmement gênant, mais c'est un léger bug.

[A] Je possède 11 Mo de mémoire (2Mo 16bits CHIP et 9Mo 32Bits FAST et EXT),
    je me suis donc permis de mettre un tampon de 2Mo. Et là surprise 2
    plantages au bout de la 3ème ou 4ème disquettes !!

